<section id="A3.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.2 </span>Transformer Params</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the Transformer models, we assume the Llama architecture with Grouped-Query Attention from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grattafiori et al. (2024)</a></cite> and count the parameters in Tab. <a href="#A3.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ C.1.2 Transformer Params ‣ C.1 Parameter Counts ‣ Appendix C Accounting: Parameters, Cache Sizes, FLOPs, Memory Operations ‣ xLSTM Scaling Laws: Competitive Performance with Linear Time-Complexity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span> <span id="A3.T6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter counts</span> for the <span id="A3.T6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Transformer Self-Attention Model</span>.</figcaption>
<div id="A3.T6.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:450.2pt;height:172.2pt;vertical-align:-83.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<p id="A3.T6.6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T6.6.1.1" class="ltx_text">
